      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subject offered key: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\n- subject title: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- offering department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- term description: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- rank of each subject within its offering department: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- course number: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER\n- course number description: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER_DESC\n- number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- reserve catalog key: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY\n- dense rank over the material status key: LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n- start date of the term: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_START_DATE\n- end date of the term: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_END_DATE\n- description \"Fall Term 2024-2025\": ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_DESCRIPTION\n- more than 0 enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- material status key of 'U': LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_CODE\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each subject offered in the term with the description \"Fall Term 2024-2025\", show the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, and the rank of each subject within its offering department ordered by subject offered key.\n```sql\nSELECT t0.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY, t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ORDER BY t0.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY) AS window_column FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE JOIN ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION = 'Fall Term 2024-2025'\n```\n2. List the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, and the reserve catalog key for each subject, along with dense ranks over the material status key ordered by material status key, for subjects that have more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U'.\n```sql\nSELECT t1.COURSE_NUMBER, t1.COURSE_NUMBER_DESC, t1.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t2.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY, DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t2.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY ORDER BY t2.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) AS window_column FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 JOIN LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL t2 ON t1.SUBJECT_ID = t2.SUBJECT_ID WHERE t1.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND t2.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'\n```\n3. For each subject offered in the term with the description \"Fall Term 2024-2025\" that also has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', show the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the rank of each subject within its offering department, the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, the reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, with the columns listed in that order.\n```sql\nWITH SubjectOfferedInTerm AS ( SELECT t0.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY, t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ORDER BY t0.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY) AS window_column, t0.SUBJECT_ID FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE JOIN ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER t2 ON t1.TERM_CODE = t2.TERM_CODE WHERE t1.TERM_DESCRIPTION = 'Fall Term 2024-2025' ), LibrarySubjectWithReserve AS ( SELECT t1.COURSE_NUMBER, t1.COURSE_NUMBER_DESC, t1.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t2.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY, DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t2.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY ORDER BY t2.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY) AS window_column, t1.SUBJECT_ID FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 JOIN LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL t2 ON t1.SUBJECT_ID = t2.SUBJECT_ID WHERE t1.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND t2.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U' ) SELECT s.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY, s.SUBJECT_TITLE, s.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s.TERM_DESCRIPTION, s.window_column AS subject_rank_in_dept, l.COURSE_NUMBER, l.COURSE_NUMBER_DESC, l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, l.LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY, l.window_column AS dense_rank_material_status FROM SubjectOfferedInTerm s JOIN LibrarySubjectWithReserve l ON s.SUBJECT_ID = l.SUBJECT_ID ORDER BY s.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY, l.COURSE_NUMBER;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each subject offered in the term with the description \"Fall Term 2024-2025\" that also has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', show the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the rank of each subject within its offering department, the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, the reserve catalog key, the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, and the start and end dates of the term, with the columns listed in that order. Do not return any rounded answers."
